Let the MOV demuxer add up Google's and Apple's 360 degree and stereo boxes in any order.

An MP4 or MOV can say twice how its pictures wrap around the viewer and how they hold two eyes'
views: in Google's st3d and sv3d boxes, or its older spherical uuid box, and in Apple's vexu box,
with its proj, eyes and pack boxes, beside hfov. FFmpeg's own muxer writes both sets into an MP4
under -strict unofficial. The demuxer read both into the same AVSphericalMapping and AVStereo3D,
so whichever came later won, and each order went wrong in its own way. A proj box after sv3d
replaced the mapping, losing its yaw, pitch and roll and leaking it. An sv3d box after proj
leaked Apple's mapping. An eyes box set the packing to unspecified over the one st3d or a pack
box gave. An st3d box after eyes failed the whole header with AVERROR_INVALIDDATA, so a file
FFmpeg 6.1 opens no longer opened.

The demuxer now keeps what Apple's boxes say apart and adds it to Google's once the header is
read, so the order of the boxes no longer matters. Google's mapping is kept when there is one,
because it states the projection and also the turn and any bounds or padding, which Apple's proj
box has no room for; Apple's projection is used when there is not. Apple's primary eye, baseline
and disparity adjustment join Google's packing when the two agree, which is when Apple's boxes
say both views, not reversed, packed the same way or in a way they do not say. When they
disagree, Google's stereo description is kept whole, as VLC, which reads only Google's boxes,
shows it. The field of view describes the lens rather than the views and joins either way. A
file with one set of boxes reads as before, except that an eyes box no longer overwrites a pack
box's packing, and nothing leaks.

Applied by BuildFFmpegTask before configure, after 0008. Fixes yuroyami/KiteFFmpeg#160.

